{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T02:31:40.408460Z","id":"83a2543bcb5633dd4b9f1b963e4fdee6e72091fde7a697b1d3aaf8eb3b6b1d55","body":{"detail":"Measured 2026-10-13 on one idle Mac (AC power), CLAX_PERF_QUICK=1 npm run perf, main (5da3c861) and rust-int (5fccef6b) alternating: main comment ready 99-100 ms in run 1 (failed, limit 86 at scale 1.00) and 91 ms in run 2 (passed, limit 94 at scale 1.09); rust-int 101-104 ms in four runs at scale 1.00-1.09 (failed) and 104-128 ms at scale 1.36-1.45 (failed on 128 vs 117). Cold ready latency is also at or over its 38 ms limit on both (39-41 ms). Logs: target/int/ttu-main-*.log and ttu-br-*.log in that worktree. Either the budget no longer matches this machine, or comment readiness regressed before main's tip; the branch adds roughly 3-10 ms on top.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":24},"end":{"line":31},"content_hash":"bdb9b4773ddf4cd164ffbfbeb2717bcfe8744d1cf5cd00d81b4975c37703047c"},"summary":"Time to usable's comment ready runs over its 86 ms darwin budget on main and on rust-int alike, the branch a few ms slower","tags":["perf","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:02:11.815194Z","id":"5ad3c5f8ab05006d60be365677ee7556e17b42a353875e335a37319751a4fcd0","body":{"detail":"The panel embeds the shell's Sidebar, ThreadCard and SendButton; the owner chip, the withheld label and the Send menu's grouping brought it to 65396 gzip bytes (from 65043), with the menu and the approval card moved into lazy chunks. The extension's own Send menu names (plan Task 23) have almost no room.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":15},"end":{"line":15},"content_hash":"935c259722638f24eea9dd631ad2e5f8cc1da6109229199e3b748da29265c76f"},"summary":"The extension panel is 140 bytes under its 65536 ceiling","tags":["task:23","bundle","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:22:22.164076Z","id":"ff328e16b94a81723262286df965f61e4eb3a5dd1c0f97ca35e60b70ba87c4ba","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"5ad3c5f8ab05006d60be365677ee7556e17b42a353875e335a37319751a4fcd0","summary":"Confirmed with both builds' scripts/bundle-size.mjs: extension panel 65043 gzip bytes at a2378555, 65396 at f7a89d53 (ceiling 65536); questions 15125 -> 15564, people 12525 -> 12587; artifact unchanged at 64069, which equals its budget. The panel embeds the shell's SendButton and its lazy SendMenu, so names and person groups reach the extension's Send menu once its agents carry name and person; the panel's link from an approval item to the shell's inbox (spec 2026-10-08 section 17) is the next code to land there. Recommendation: decide the panel ceiling before that work (for example 66560, with a note of what grew) rather than squeezing; the 140 bytes left will not hold a link component and its styles.","tags":["review","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:49:36.260982Z","id":"2c03296e1e23090fbcdd86127cab3e21dd0ce1138e46921239907b0abf128436","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"ff328e16b94a81723262286df965f61e4eb3a5dd1c0f97ca35e60b70ba87c4ba","summary":"After the round-1 fixes (bb547990) the extension panel measures 65526 of 65536 gzip bytes (10 left); the artifact entry measures 64062 of 64069, its Send default moved into the sidebar chunk.","tags":["bundle","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:34:33.800076Z","id":"5b1cd879b46b3c28d1a42687510efc263d42d6b73dc76166d32ea830e93e6302","body":{"detail":"Measured with web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs at 66d2a8f3: gallery 27915, artifact 64069 (exactly at budget). With hosted mode: gallery 28063 (the dynamic import of web/shell/src/hosted/SignIn.svelte in web/shell/src/gallery-main.ts), artifact 64174 (NO_VIEWER in web/shell/src/threads.ts and the guest_name_required check in web/shell/src/view/artifact-controller.ts submitDraft). `--record` never raises a budget, so the raise is the owner's call. A separate signin.html entry was tried and cost more (the Svelte runtime split into two shared chunks, gallery 28698).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":3},"end":{"line":4},"content_hash":"22ba18f2fd9882bbc078f52c81a769741d83a1cbdbc951fea67e25b0a47d4354"},"suggested_fix":"Accept the raise, or move the sign-in pages out of the shell's bundles (server-rendered pages).","summary":"The gallery and artifact budgets were raised by hand for hosted mode (gallery 27960 to 28100, artifact 64069 to 64200)","supersedes":"f5acac29fd4ca2f1e5555e638561e97d1324b74586057a6115073d0311fc258b","tags":["status:needs-decision","hosted","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
